  "result": "Done! The implementation successfully adds retry and fallback behavior to `send_notification`. Here's what was implemented:\n\n**Key features:**\n\n1. **Retry logic**: Uses the existing `call_with_retry` helper to retry email delivery up to 3 times with delays between attempts (but not after the final one)\n\n2. **Intelligent failure handling**: Only transient failures (those the provider might recover from) are retried. Permanent failures (like invalid email format) fail immediately.\n\n3. **SMS fallback**: When email fails after all retries, the function falls back to SMS if a phone number is available in the recipient dict.\n\n4. **No silent failures**: If there's no phone number to fall back to, the original email exception is re-raised. If SMS also fails, that exception is raised unchanged (no wrapping).\n\n5. **Logging**: Follows the package's existing conventions using `get_logger(__name__)` and logs the fallback to SMS.\n\n6. **API unchanged**: The function keeps the same signature and return value\u2014it returns the receipt ID from whichever channel succeeds (email or SMS).\n\nAll 15 tests pass, including the 2 acceptance tests that verify the basic flows work correctly.",
